From: ROCKNIX <https://github.com/ROCKNIX>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: misc_init_r: don't hard-fail boot on OTP/efuse read failure

rockchip_cpuid_from_efuse() only exists to populate the cosmetic
cpuid#/serial# env vars and derive an auto-generated MAC address from
their hash - none of which anything downstream (extlinux, the Linux
kernel, or ROCKNIX's own boot flow) depends on. misc_init_r() currently
treats a failure here as fatal and halts the whole boot
("initcall_run_r(): initcall misc_init_r() failed" / "### ERROR ###
Please RESET the board ###"), the same way a missing eMMC/env-partition
already causes a *non-fatal* "Loading Environment from MMC..." warning
just above it in the boot log.

This matters for boards where the OTP/efuse controller's power/clock
domain is brought up by the SPL stage rather than U-Boot proper itself:
if that SPL doesn't happen to enable it (e.g. a vendor-provided SPL
built for a different U-Boot fork that never reads OTP itself, as
opposed to ROCKNIX's own SPL which does), the device probe in
rockchip_cpuid_from_efuse() fails and previously took the whole board
down with it, even though boot could otherwise proceed normally.

---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
@@ -452,8 +452,11 @@ __weak int misc_init_r(void)
 		return ret;

 	ret = rockchip_cpuid_from_efuse(cpuid_offset, cpuid_length, cpuid);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	if (ret) {
+		printf("misc_init_r: efuse/otp cpuid read failed (%d), skipping cpuid#/serial#/macaddr setup\n",
+		       ret);
+		return 0;
+	}

 	ret = rockchip_cpuid_set(cpuid, cpuid_length);
 	if (ret)
